# Lain source text must stay LF on every platform.
#
# The seed C parser and the frozen bootstrap frontend scan source text by \n,
# and `run_lainir_self_host.py` asserts that the split parts reconstruct
# `seed/lainir/compiler.l1` byte-for-byte.  With core.autocrlf=true and no
# explicit attribute, Git rewrites these files to CRLF on checkout, so the
# working tree would depend on which tool wrote a file last and the
# reconstruction assertion would fail on a mixed tree.
*.l1 text eol=lf
*.lain text eol=lf
